this church is now  home for hundreds of people who fled  mount neregongo  africa's most active volcano  some of their homes were destroyed by an  eruption last week  others followed the army's order to then  evacuate the city of gomer  in the democratic republic of congo  esperanza mushika  is one of several people here who told  us they lost their children  in the panic i was on my way out to buy  flour when i saw the fire  my children were out playing we all ran  away i don't know where they went  later i was told they were in a car  accident trying to escape  but i can't find them in the hospitals  or morgues they were declared missing  and i'm yet to find them  it's got to be hard to find anyone here  in the town of sake  it's overrun just down the road from the  church these people are waiting for food  it's the first help they've been given  since they arrived four days ago  right now the level of the crisis  is high because people have gone without  food  they have been relying on others to help  them  they are hungry people  they're thirsty too there's just  this one water point that's now being  shared by hundreds of people  they're queuing up waiting their turn to  try and get water to drink  and for cooking the conditions aren't  really clean at all here  the latrines that belong to the local  community aren't nearly enough  for all the people that have arrived  here the local administrator has said  that they've already detected  several cases of cholera meanwhile  esperanza has found a glimmer of hope  somebody called her from gomer saying  they've seen her children  near her home it's a 20 kilometer ride  back to the city  rocks formed from lava from past  eruptions  cover her neighborhood it's near the  foot of the volcano  in the red zone not a safe place  for missing children in an eruption  but she's in luck  i have so many things to say i'm happy  to see them and i'm grateful they're  alive  they didn't die  one family happily reunited  many more are still not malcolm webb  al jazeera gomer democratic republic of  congo
 

